WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 12 Leader Video
Unit 3, Lesson 4: Designer

1
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.840
So we've almost made it through science.

2
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:13.660
Now, we've discovered that science is really a foundation for understanding our

3
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.460
world, and it does not contradict our faith.

4
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:22.280
Well, that's good news. We've also taken a look at three really good pieces of

5
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:28.220
evidence that help us see that God is actually there, that we have evidence for

6
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:34.020
God. We looked at the idea of fine-tuning we looked at the idea

7
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:39.520
of DNA and we looked at the idea of design all of these

8
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.520
pointing to God in some way shape or form through the use of science

9
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:50.100
now I want you to keep in mind two kinds of students this week

10
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:55.840
the first kind is the student that has all this information and is super fired up

11
00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.940
and ready to go with the best arguments that they have to their teacher who probably

12
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.000
knows more than they do about all these things, especially this week with the idea

13
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
of design because this is where the conversation between creation and evolution

14
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.000
starts to really come alive. And it might seem like this is

15
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.360
a good idea for them to jump off and start all these arguments and try to win people

16
00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.000
to Christ and they might try it, and you want to champion that.

17
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:29.820
But at the same time, make sure that they do so in truth and love.

18
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.360
That if they're going to have these conversations, you don't want to tell them not

19
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.240
to. And it's okay that they can challenge their teachers, and it's okay to challenge

20
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.160
their students. But to do so with love, and to do so with the appropriate amount of

21
00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:46.200
respect, especially for teachers, as well as engaging in the right kinds of

22
00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.580
conversations. Now, the other type of student is maybe the one that really is still

23
00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:55.940
not sure or the one that wasn't sure before entering into this conversation.

24
00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.460
Now would be a really good time to take a step back and take inventory with that

25
00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:06.220
student and ask them just the plain question, was this enough evidence?

26
00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.680
Do you need more? What further questions do you have?

27
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.600
What clarifications do you need?

28
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.380
Now remember the reason and why we're doing this study.

29
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.940
It's so that our students can have a deep conviction for themselves about what they

30
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.240
believe and why they believe it.

31
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:27.660
And to also be able to communicate that in love and humility and do so relationally.

32
00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:33.500
So while it might be really exciting to have some eager students to get started and

33
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.440
to get engaged in conversation,

34
00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.720
help them be patient because there is so much more to learn.

